%description:
LTE AM polling (TS 36.322 5.2.2): the transmitting AM entity sets the poll bit P in an
AMD PDU when PDU_WITHOUT_POLL >= pollPDU, BYTE_WITHOUT_POLL >= pollByte, or the buffer
empties / the window stalls; POLL_SN is recorded and t-PollRetransmit is (re)started.

FAITHFUL ASSERTION: at least one LTE AMD PDU on the wire carries P=1.

[NOT-MODELED] Simu5G's LTE AM data PDU (LteRlcAmPdu) has NO poll/P field at all: LTE AM
retransmission is driven by a local per-PDU timer and STATUS is emitted on an ad-hoc
interval, not by spec polling + t-PollRetransmit + t-StatusProhibit
(RLC-spec-gap-analysis.md #4). The predicate lteAmHasPollBit() is therefore always false,
the step never matches, and the program FAILs -- reported by opp_test as EXPECTEDFAIL (via
the expected-failure directive below). If Simu5G later adds an LTE poll field, this becomes
a real PASS.

%file: Lte_Am_PollBit.cc

#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "Simu5gRlcTestSupport.h"

namespace inet { namespace protocoltest {

using namespace rlctest;

Define_ProtocolTest(lte_am_poll_bit)
{
    return ProtocolTest("lte_am_poll_bit")
        .once(on("eNB.cellularNic.rlcMux").signal("sentPacketToLowerLayer")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c){ return isLteAmData(c) && lteAmHasPollBit(c); })
                  .describe("an LTE AMD PDU with the poll bit set").within(2.5));
}

} } // namespace

%inifile: test.ini
[General]
include ../../ini/_lte.ini
*.tester.testName = "lte_am_poll_bit"
**.cellularNic.ip2nic.conversationalRlc = "AM"

%expected-failure: Simu5G LTE AM has no poll (P) field (RLC-spec-gap-analysis.md #4) -- NOT-MODELED

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST lte_am_poll_bit: PASS
